<!--
  Both language versions of every page, paired with xhtml:link alternates.

  hreflang has to be BIDIRECTIONAL to count: a page declaring an alternate that
  does not declare it back is ignored. Until now only the Russian pages carried
  the tags — the English originals had none at all — so the pairing was
  one-directional and search engines were entitled to disregard it entirely.
  The English pages now carry their own, and this file states the pairs a third
  time, which is the form Yandex reads most reliably.

  /en/ is deliberately absent: it duplicates "/" and is disallowed in robots.txt.
  watch.html has no Russian alternate — /ru/watch.html rewrites to this same
  English page, so claiming a "ru" version would point at English content.
  /app/ is an install helper, not a page anyone should reach from a search.

  No <lastmod>: it would be a hardcoded date going quietly stale, which is worse
  than omitting an optional field. <changefreq> and <priority> are omitted for
  the same reason — both are hints crawlers now largely ignore.
-->
